window.KS_CAPS=[[0.6, 5.04, "After heavy rain, a cocoa grower has about thirty minutes to scout."], [5.09, 7.0, "Which blocks should they check first?"], [7.05, 11.08, "Guess wrong, and black pod spreads to healthy pods."], [12.3, 18.55, "Black pod spreads by rain splash and costs an estimated twenty to thirty percent of global cocoa production."], [18.6, 23.21, "Heavy rain is already linked to lower yields in Ghana, Ecuador and Indonesia."], [23.26, 31.21, "In Malaysia, eighty-six percent of cocoa land is smallholdings, and advisers can't visit every farm after every storm."], [32.02, 36.05, "Growers already have photo apps, forecasts and paper logs."], [36.1, 41.22, "But none of them turns \"it rained heavily\" into \"walk these blocks first, in the time you have\"."], [41.27, 45.0, "That empty corner is where KokoShield sits."], [45.68, 53.68, "KokoShield Field Desk combines the rain reading, the block map and past cases into a ranked route that fits thirty minutes."], [53.73, 58.31, "Every stop shows why it's there, on a phone or a printed checklist."], [60.02, 63.72, "Scouts log each suspected pod with a note and a photo."], [63.77, 69.82, "An adviser then confirms or rules out every case, so only verified disease counts."], [70.6, 73.86, "Our pilot runs on one cocoa farm in Tanjung Sepat."], [73.91, 79.15, "Two scouts walk the same thirty minutes: one on the ranked route, one on the usual round."], [79.2, 81.68, "A follow-up check counts what each missed."], [81.73, 86.81, "We go ahead only if the ranked route finds more confirmed pods per hour in three of four rounds."], [86.86, 89.97, "The pilot budget is twelve hundred ringgit."], [90.86, 95.6, "Finding disease sooner means fewer pods lost, and treatment only where it's needed."], [95.65, 97.83, "Growers use KokoShield for free."], [97.88, 106.6, "A cooperative or buyer pays seventy-five ringgit per farm per season, starting with a twenty-farm cluster in Sabah or Sarawak in 2027."], [107.37, 109.91, "We're a team of five from Universiti Malaya."], [109.96, 118.41, "KokoShield helps cocoa growers find disease sooner after the rain: one farm first, then every cocoa region facing wetter seasons."]];
